      "PROVENANCE.md": "# Provenance\n\n`design-taste-frontend` is an OpenCorvus adaptation of the Massachusetts Institute of Technology (MIT) licensed Taste Skill by Leonxlnx.\n\nSources reviewed on 2026-08-03:\n\n- Repository and installation documentation: <https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill>\n- Default v2 Skill: <https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill/blob/main/skills/taste-skill/SKILL.md>\n- Generative Pre-trained Transformer (GPT) oriented variant: <https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill/blob/main/skills/gpt-tasteskill/SKILL.md>\n- Upstream MIT license: <https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill/blob/main/LICENSE>\n\nThe adaptation retains the upstream ideas of brief inference, contextual design dials, anti-template bias correction, mature design-system selection, intentional hierarchy and motion, redesign audit, and rendered pre-flight inspection.\n\nIt replaces upstream framework, marketing-page, mobile, dark-mode, asset-placeholder, fallback, and simulated-randomization defaults with OpenCorvus contracts. The resulting Skill supports product interfaces such as Prism's dense financial surfaces while preserving the active Expert Squad, Product Requirements, evidence, platform, and design-system authority.\n",
